      {
        "id": 234386,
        "name": "drezzinator",
        "username": "drezzinator",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/bc8723/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2020-12-15T08:12:34.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Minion Maker would in fact be able to keep making minions. Keep in mind though that its only 1 per turn (usually), and most scene trackers are on average 8, so really theres a functional ceiling there. Also the player minions can die relatively easily so by the time you get to 8, some have probably died and you're probably around 4-6 at that time.</p>\n<p>I think the Side Kick thing is more of a reference to the \"development\" part of the statement, and not part of the \"helper\" part of the statement. As a GM, if my player really wanted a permanent side kick, I would find a house rule that would work both for the player and the character's story. I'd probably then also scale the enemies accordingly (if needed).</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
