      {
        "id": 234391,
        "name": "der andere Jan",
        "username": "der_andere_Jan",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/der_andere_jan/{size}/1881_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-12-15T23:37:50.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Generally, even within the 'balanced' creation method, you're encouraged to interprete and rename any Power as you see fit.</p>\n<p>Gravity Control, for example, is not mentioned separately, but certainly Cosmic&nbsp;Power is close enough.</p>\n<p>Missing Machine Empathy? Either take Robotics, or Animal Control - depending how you are planning to play it.</p>\n<p>And then rename it according to your narrative!&nbsp;</p>\n<p>For your bunch of Minions, I'd suggest Robotics renamed to 'Bunch o' Minions', or Part Detachment, or whatever you come up with that somehow, if barely, fits the bill.</p>\n<p>The re-interpretation aspect of Hero creation puts a lot of power into our hands, without much need of making houserules.</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:10:28.536Z",
